-- methods, abilities (traits), generics
record Account:
    owner as text
    balance as number

to Account's deposit amount as number changes me:
    increase my balance by amount

to Account's can_afford price as number gives truth:
    give back my balance is at least price

to Account's describe gives text:
    give back "{my owner} has {my balance}"

let changeable acc be Account with owner "Sushant", balance 100
acc's deposit with 50
say acc's describe
say "can afford 120? {acc's can_afford with 120}"
say "can afford 500? {acc's can_afford with 500}"

ability Shape:
    to area gives number
    to label gives text:
        give back "a shape with area {me's area}"

record Square:
    side as number

record Circle:
    radius as number

to Square's area gives number:
    give back my side * my side

to Circle's area gives number:
    give back round with 3.14159 * my radius * my radius, 2

to Circle's label gives text:
    give back "a circle of radius {my radius}"

Square can Shape
Circle can Shape

to total_area shapes as list of Shape gives number:
    let changeable sum be 0
    for each s in shapes:
        increase sum by s's area
    give back sum

let shapes as list of Shape be list of (Square with side 2), (Circle with radius 1)
for each s in shapes:
    say s's label
say "total area: {total_area with shapes}"

-- generics
record Pair of A and B:
    left as A
    right as B

to swap p as Pair of A and B gives Pair of B and A:
    give back Pair with left p's right, right p's left

let p be Pair with left 1, right "one"
let q be swap with p
say "swapped: {q's left}, {q's right}"

to first_or items as list of T, fallback as T gives T:
    if length of items is 0:
        give back fallback
    give back item 1 of items

say first_or with (list of 4, 5), 0
say first_or with (empty list), "none"

choice Tree:
    Leaf
    Node with value as number, left as Tree, right as Tree

to Tree's total gives number:
    when me:
        is Leaf: give back 0
        is Node with v, l, r: give back v + l's total + r's total

let tree be Node with value 1, left (Node with value 2, left Leaf, right Leaf), right Leaf
say "tree total: {tree's total}"

-- a method without inputs, called on its own line, that replaces `me`
record Gauge:
    level as number

to Gauge's reset changes me:
    change me to Gauge with level 0

let changeable g be Gauge with level 9
g's reset
say "gauge after reset: {g's level}"
